Ladybird hands every process hosting a frame of a tab the tab’s
User-Agent and settings. WebKit’s WebPageProxy::setUserAgent() sends
SetUserAgent to each of the page’s processes with
forEachWebContentProcess(); Chromium’s WebContentsImpl::
SyncRendererPrefs() broadcasts the RendererPreferences, the
user_agent_override among them, to every RenderViewHost of the
WebContents; and Gecko keeps the override in BrowsingContext’s synced
UserAgentOverride field, which every process holding the context gets.
All three reach a cross-site iframe’s process, as Ladybird now does.
